<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lippstadt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lippstadt is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the Lippe, founded around 1185 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-ii-of-lippe">Bernhard II of Lippe</a> as one of the first planned towns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>. A Hanseatic town, it was for centuries ruled jointly by the lords of Lippe and the counts of the Mark and their successors. Today it is an industrial centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lippstadt.jpg" alt="Lippstadt" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lippstadt_in_SO.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
